\"text-align:center\"><span style=\"color:#ccc\">&mdash;</span></td></tr><tr style=\"opacity:.5\"><td style=\"font-weight:400\">Merav Ribeiro</td><td style=\"font-size:.78rem\">Chief Innovation Officer</td><td style=\"font-size:.75rem;color:#666\">Principal</td><td style=\"text-align:center\"><span style=\"color:#ccc\">&mdash;</span></td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-weight:600\">Clifton Solis</td><td style=\"font-size:.78rem\">Manager of Business Intelligence</td><td style=\"font-size:.75rem;color:#666\">Advisor</td><td style=\"text-align:center\"><span style=\"color:#15803d;font-weight:700\">&#10003;</span></td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-weight:600\">Ryan Goodman</td><td style=\"font-size:.78rem\">Director of Legislative Affairs</td><td style=\"font-size:.75rem;color:#666\">Carve-Out Advisor (External)</td><td style=\"text-align:center\"><span style=\"color:#15803d;font-weight:700\">&#10003;</span></td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-weight:600\">Johann Cortez</td><td style=\"font-size:.78rem\">Director of Accounting Operations</td><td style=\"font-size:.75rem;color:#666\">Product Strategy Advisor (External)</td><td style=\"text-align:center\"><span style=\"color:#15803d;font-weight:700\">&#10003;</span></td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"mb-4\"><h5 style=\"font-weight:800;color:var(--navy);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em;font-size:.8rem;margin-bottom:1rem;padding-bottom:.5rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--gold)\">Agenda</h5><div style=\"margin-bottom:1.5rem;padding-bottom:1.25rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)\"><div style=\"font-size:.68rem;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.1em;color:#999;margin-bottom:.2rem\">Item 1</div><h6 style=\"font-size:.92rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.6rem\">Ethics and Compliance Program Annual Report</h6><p style=\"font-size:.87rem;line-height:1.7;color:#333;margin-bottom:0\">A presentation on the Ethics and Compliance Program Annual Report was given by Johann Cortez, our external advisor from ACPWB. The presentation benchmarked Aspire Talent Group&#x27;s practices against 36 peers in the Responsible AI Governance sector. The committee directed management to develop an action plan based on the findings.</p></div><div style=\"margin-bottom:1.5rem;padding-bottom:1.25rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)\"><div style=\"font-size:.68rem;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.1em;color:#999;margin-bottom:.2rem\">Item 2</div><h6 style=\"font-size:.92rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.6rem\">Job Architecture Redesign — Phase 2 Approval</h6><p style=\"font-size:.87rem;line-height:1.7;color:#333;margin-bottom:0\">The Job Architecture Redesign — Phase 2 Approval was a review of the company&#x27;s real estate portfolio. The committee approved a plan to consolidate 36 office locations, resulting in an estimated annual savings of $36M.</p><div style=\"background:#f8f9fb;border:1px solid var(--border);border-left:3px solid var(--navy);padding:.8rem 1rem;margin-top:.65rem\"><div style=\"font-size:.62rem;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.1em;color:#888;margin-bottom:.4rem\">Motion</div><p style=\"margin-bottom:.4rem;font-size:.83rem;line-height:1.6;color:#333\"><strong>To approve for partnership:</strong> RESOLVED, that the Manufacturing Excellence Committee establishes an ad hoc subcommittee to further investigate the Job Architecture Redesign — Phase 2 Approval and report its findings back to the full committee within 90 days.</p><div style=\"font-size:.8rem;color:#555;margin-bottom:.3rem\"><strong>Moved:</strong> Ilaria Chala &nbsp;&bull;&nbsp; <strong>Seconded:</strong> Clifton Solis</div><div style=\"font-size:.8rem;color:#555\"><strong>Vote:</strong> 5 Yea &nbsp;/&nbsp; 1 Nay &nbsp;/&nbsp; 0 Abstain &nbsp;&mdash;&nbsp; <strong style=\"color:#15803d\">CARRIED</strong></div></div></div><div style=\"margin-bottom:1.5rem;padding-bottom:1.25rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)\"><div style=\"font-size:.68rem;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.1em;color:#999;margin-bottom:.2rem\">Item 3</div><h6 style=\"font-size:.92rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.6rem\">Stock Ownership Guideline Compliance Review</h6><p style=\"font-size:.87rem;line-height:1.7;color:#333;margin-bottom:0\">The Stock Ownership Guideline Compliance Review was a review of the company&#x27;s compliance with the Dodd-Frank Act. The committee reviewed the company&#x27;s executive compensation practices and confirmed that they were in compliance.</p><div style=\"background:#f8f9fb;border:1px solid var(--border);border-left:3px solid var(--navy);padding:.8rem 1rem;margin-top:.65rem\"><div style=\"font-size:.62rem;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.1em;color:#888;margin-bottom:.4rem\">Motion</div><p style=\"margin-bottom:.4rem;font-size:.83rem;line-height:1.6;color:#333\"><strong>To table:</strong> RESOLVED, that the Manufacturing Excellence Committee approves the formation of a new subsidiary, Aspire Talent Group, to pursue the Stock Ownership Guideline Compliance Review.</p><div style=\"font-size:.8rem;color:#555;margin-bottom:.3rem\"><strong>Moved:</strong> Chinonso Truong &nbsp;&bull;&nbsp; <strong>Seconded:</strong> Ilaria Chala</div><div style=\"font-size:.8rem;color:#555\"><strong>Vote:</strong> 5 Yea &nbsp;/&nbsp; 0 Nay &nbsp;/&nbsp; 1 Abstain &nbsp;&mdash;&nbsp; <strong style=\"color:#15803d\">CARRIED</strong></div></div></div><div style=\"margin-bottom:1.5rem;padding-bottom:1.25rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)\"><div style=\"font-size:.68rem;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.1em;color:#999;margin-bottom:.2rem\">Item 4</div><h6 style=\"font-size:.92rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.6rem\">Customer Advisory Board Feedback Summary</h6><p style=\"font-size:.87rem;line-height:1.7;color:#333;margin-bottom:0\">A special session was held to review the Customer Advisory Board Feedback Summary. Aroha Fischer outlined the strategic rationale for the proposal, emphasizing the competitive pressures in the Responsible AI Governance sector. The committee members questioned the financial assumptions and requested additional sensitivity analysis before the next meeting.</p></div></div><div class=\"mb-4\"><h5 style=\"font-weight:800;color:var(--navy);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em;font-size:.8rem;margin-bottom:1rem;padding-bottom:.5rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--gold)\">Action Items</h5><table class=\"dash-table w-100\"><thead><tr><th style=\"width:2rem\">#</th><th>Description</th><th>Owner</th><th>Due</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style=\"color:#999;font-weight:600\">1</td><td style=\"font-size:.83rem\">Prepare board-level summary of Ethics and Compliance Program Annual Report for inclusion in quarterly reporting package</td><td style=\"font-size:.78rem;font-weight:600;white-space:nowrap\">Jesse Jacobs</td><td style=\"font-size:.72rem;color:#666;white-space:nowrap\">1987-04-28</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#999;font-weight:600\">2</td><td style=\"font-size:.83rem\">Develop a plan for improving the company&#x27;s innovation pipeline</td><td style=\"font-size:.78rem;font-weight:600;white-space:nowrap\">Yaw Buenaventura</td><td style=\"font-size:.72rem;color:#666;white-space:nowrap\">1987-03-28</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#999;font-weight:600\">3</td><td style=\"font-size:.83rem\">Prepare a summary of the company&#x27;s real estate lease obligations</td><td style=\"font-size:.78rem;font-weight:600;white-space:nowrap\">Gabriela Church</td><td style=\"font-size:.72rem;color:#666;white-space:nowrap\">1987-04-28</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#999;font-weight:600\">4</td><td style=\"font-size:.83rem\">Organize a board education session on emerging ESG trends</td><td style=\"font-size:.78rem;font-weight:600;white-space:nowrap\">Norzaidi Atkins</td><td style=\"font-size:.72rem;color:#666;white-space:nowrap\">1987-03-28</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div style=\"border:1px solid var(--border);padding:1rem 1.2rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem\"><p style=\"font-size:.85rem;color:#333;line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.5rem\">There being no further business, a motion to adjourn was made and carried unanimously. Meeting adjourned at 1:00 PM CT.</p><p style=\"font-size:.83rem;margin-bottom:.75rem;color:#555\"><strong>Next meeting:</strong> 1987-03-12</p><div><p style=\"font-size:.78rem;color:#888;margin-bottom:.25rem\">Respectfully submitted,</p><p style=\"font-size:.85rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.1rem\">Johann Cortez</p><p style=\"font-size:.78rem;color:#666;margin-bottom:.75rem\">Director of Accounting Operations, Product Strategy Advisor (External)</p><div style=\"display:flex;gap:2rem\"><div><div style=\"width:160px;border-bottom:1px solid #aaa;margin-bottom:.2rem;height:1.5rem\"></div><div style=\"font-size:.68rem;color:#888\">Signature</div></div><div><div style=\"width:120px;border-bottom:1px solid #aaa;margin-bottom:.2rem;height:1.5rem\"></div><div style=\"font-size:.68rem;color:#888\">Approved: ___________</div></div></div></div></div><div style=\"display:flex;justify-content:space-between;padding-top:1rem;border-top:1px solid var(--border)\"><a href=\"/archive/1987/02/27/key-person-and-corporate-owned-life-insurance-review-9355/\" style=\"font-size:.85rem;color:var(--muted);text-decoration:none\">&larr; Previous</a><a href=\"/archive/1987/02/28/legal/settlement-summary-8890/midstream-pipeline-management-compensation-9576/\" style=\"font-size:.85rem;color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none\">Next &rarr;</a></div></div><div class=\"col-lg-4 d-none d-lg-block\"><div style=\"position:sticky;top:2rem\"><div class=\"acpwb-card mb-3\"><div style=\"font-size:.65rem;font-weight:800;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.1em;color:var(--gold);margin-bottom:.7rem\">Meeting Record</div><dl class=\"mb-0\" style=\"font-size:.82rem\"><dt style=\"opacity:.55;font-size:.